load @term/seed/structure/set
  find set

# A finite automaton: the simplest machine, a finite set of states reading an input symbol by symbol, jumping between
# states by a transition rule, accepting if it ends in an accepting state. It has no memory beyond its current state,
# and what it recognizes is exactly the regular languages, the bottom of the Chomsky hierarchy. The form carries the set
# of states and the input alphabet; the transition rule and accepting states are the machine.
form finite-automaton
  link states, like set
  link alphabet, like set
